<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE reference PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Reference//EN" "reference.dtd">
<reference id="service-configuration-reference" xml:lang="en">
<title><ph keyref="service">Lattice Relay</ph> configuration reference</title>
<shortdesc>Every key of <codeph>relay.yaml</codeph>, the commands of the <codeph>{{cli}}</codeph> tool that manage a relay, the states a delivery goes through, and the limits of a project. Fictional sample written for this portfolio.</shortdesc>
<refbody>
<section><title>The configuration file</title>
<p><codeph>relay.yaml</codeph> is read at deployment. A key that isn't listed here makes the deployment fail with <codeph>unknown key</codeph>, so a typo can't silently do nothing.</p>
</section>
<section><title>Top level</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Key</stentry><stentry>Type</stentry><stentry>Required</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>version</codeph></stentry><stentry>integer</stentry><stentry>Yes</stentry><stentry>The format of the file. Only <codeph>1</codeph> exists.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>name</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry>Yes</stentry><stentry>The relay's name. Lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens, up to 40 characters.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>source</codeph></stentry><stentry>object</stentry><stentry>Yes</stentry><stentry>Where events come in. See <i>source</i>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>targets</codeph></stentry><stentry>list</stentry><stentry>Yes</stentry><stentry>Where events go. One to five entries. See <i>targets</i>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>retry</codeph></stentry><stentry>object</stentry><stentry>No</stentry><stentry>How failed deliveries are retried. See <i>retry</i>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>dead_letter</codeph></stentry><stentry>object</stentry><stentry>No</stentry><stentry>What happens to deliveries that run out of attempts. See <i>dead_letter</i>.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>source</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Key</stentry><stentry>Type</stentry><stentry>Default</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>path</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry><codeph>/hooks</codeph></stentry><stentry>The path the sender posts to. Must start with <codeph>/</codeph>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>verify</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry><codeph>none</codeph></stentry><stentry>How incoming events are checked: <codeph>none</codeph>, <codeph>hmac-sha256</codeph>, or <codeph>basic</codeph>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>secret_from</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>The environment variable that holds the secret for <codeph>hmac-sha256</codeph>, or the <codeph>user:password</codeph> pair for <codeph>basic</codeph>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>signature_header</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry><codeph>X-Signature-256</codeph></stentry><stentry>The header the sender puts the signature in.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>max_body_kb</codeph></stentry><stentry>integer</stentry><stentry><codeph>256</codeph></stentry><stentry>The largest body the relay accepts. Larger bodies get <codeph>413 Payload Too Large</codeph>.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>targets</title>
<p>Each entry in <codeph>targets</codeph> is one destination. The relay delivers every event to every target, and keeps a separate attempt count for each.</p>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Key</stentry><stentry>Type</stentry><stentry>Default</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>name</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>A label that appears in delivery listings. Unique within the file.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>url_from</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>The environment variable that holds the target's HTTPS address.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>timeout_seconds</codeph></stentry><stentry>integer</stentry><stentry><codeph>10</codeph></stentry><stentry>How long the relay waits for the target's response. 1 to 30.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>headers</codeph></stentry><stentry>map</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>Extra headers to send with every delivery. Values may name an environment variable as <codeph>${NAME}</codeph>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>success_codes</codeph></stentry><stentry>list</stentry><stentry><codeph>[200, 201, 202, 204]</codeph></stentry><stentry>The response codes that count as delivered.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>retry</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Key</stentry><stentry>Type</stentry><stentry>Default</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>max_attempts</codeph></stentry><stentry>integer</stentry><stentry><codeph>5</codeph></stentry><stentry>Attempts per target, including the first. 1 to 12.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>backoff</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry><codeph>exponential</codeph></stentry><stentry><codeph>exponential</codeph> doubles the wait from 5 seconds; <codeph>fixed</codeph> waits <codeph>interval_seconds</codeph> each time.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>interval_seconds</codeph></stentry><stentry>integer</stentry><stentry><codeph>30</codeph></stentry><stentry>The wait for <codeph>fixed</codeph> backoff.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>retry_on</codeph></stentry><stentry>list</stentry><stentry><codeph>[408, 429, 500, 502, 503, 504]</codeph></stentry><stentry>The response codes that lead to a retry. Any other failure code ends the delivery.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>dead_letter</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Key</stentry><stentry>Type</stentry><stentry>Default</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>keep_days</codeph></stentry><stentry>integer</stentry><stentry><codeph>3</codeph></stentry><stentry>How long a failed delivery is kept for replay. 0 to 30.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>notify_from</codeph></stentry><stentry>string</stentry><stentry></stentry><stentry>An environment variable with an email address to notify when a delivery fails for good.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Commands</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Command</stentry><stentry>What it does</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} deploy</codeph></stentry><stentry>Reads <codeph>relay.yaml</codeph> in the current folder and deploys it to the default project.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} env set NAME=value</codeph></stentry><stentry>Stores an environment variable, encrypted. Takes effect at the next deployment.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} env list</codeph></stentry><stentry>Lists variable names and when each was last set. Never shows values.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} deliveries list [--last N] [--state STATE]</codeph></stentry><stentry>Lists deliveries, newest first.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} deliveries show ID</codeph></stentry><stentry>Shows one delivery: every attempt, response code, and duration.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} deliveries replay ID</codeph></stentry><stentry>Sends a delivery again from the dead-letter store.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>{{cli}} logs --follow</codeph></stentry><stentry>Streams the relay's log.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Delivery states</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>State</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry><stentry>What to do</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>received</codeph></stentry><stentry>The event passed verification and is queued.</stentry><stentry>Nothing. It moves on within a second.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>delivered</codeph></stentry><stentry>A target returned a success code.</stentry><stentry>Nothing.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>retrying</codeph></stentry><stentry>A target failed with a retryable code, and another attempt is scheduled.</stentry><stentry>Check the target if it stays here for more than a few minutes.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>failed</codeph></stentry><stentry>The attempts ran out, or the target returned a code that isn't retried.</stentry><stentry>Fix the target, and then replay the delivery.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>rejected</codeph></stentry><stentry>The event failed verification, or the body was too large.</stentry><stentry>Check the sender's secret and body size. Rejected events aren't stored.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Response codes the relay returns to the sender</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Code</stentry><stentry>Meaning</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry><codeph>202 Accepted</codeph></stentry><stentry>The event is queued. The sender should treat this as success.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>401 Unauthorized</codeph></stentry><stentry>The signature or credentials didn't match.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>404 Not Found</codeph></stentry><stentry>The path doesn't match <codeph>source.path</codeph>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>413 Payload Too Large</codeph></stentry><stentry>The body exceeds <codeph>max_body_kb</codeph>.</stentry></strow><strow><stentry><codeph>429 Too Many Requests</codeph></stentry><stentry>The project is over its rate limit. The response carries a <codeph>Retry-After</codeph> header.</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
<section><title>Limits</title>
<simpletable><sthead><stentry>Limit</stentry><stentry>Developer plan</stentry><stentry>Team plan</stentry></sthead><strow><stentry>Events per minute, per project</stentry><stentry>600</stentry><stentry>6,000</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Targets per relay</stentry><stentry>2</stentry><stentry>5</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Body size</stentry><stentry>256 KB</stentry><stentry>1 MB</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Dead-letter retention</stentry><stentry>3 days</stentry><stentry>30 days</stentry></strow><strow><stentry>Relays per project</stentry><stentry>3</stentry><stentry>20</stentry></strow></simpletable>
</section>
</refbody>
</reference>
